 ### 6.4 Phases that receive
 
-- **A tile whose phase receives** arms its counters **in the start path, after GO: write the counters first (each write adds; at a phase start the count is 0), then pulse start.** Arming them during "configure" would break invariant 4 at configure's `done`; storing them before the start pulse means no arrival can beat its counter. The start path is identical code on every tile, so every tile's start store lands on the same cycle (plus skew), and its first request follows by the lead-in of 4.2. Measured from C&C's GO store to every tile's first request [meas: meshsim, L = 1]: **9–10 cycles** for a stream run started by a counter store then start (5–6 to the start store, then 2L + 2), and **17–18** for a group run on the all-to-all recipe's longer start path (10–11, then 4L + 3); a group run with the shortest start path would take 12–13 [derived from the two measured parts]. Every tile's first request lands within the 0/+1 start skew. The tile then `WFI`s for counters done (4.12) when it has nothing else to do.
